{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 18, :comments ["<b>And he does not know</b> — the simpleton who follows her [suddenly], that the dead are there, in the depths of Sheol. There her guests are called, and the word <i>sham</i> (\"there\") hints at Sheol. The first section is completed, concerning the account of the value of wisdom and its warnings and its discipline. The second section:"], :book :proverbs, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 9, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Proverbs -- Daat" "http://www.daat.ac.il/he-il/tanach/parshanut_hamikra/full-text/eben-ezra/mishley/"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T19:21:47.099871394Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}